# Current calculation: occupied-space trace on the supplied path

From this folder, run:

../../../../build/vaspberry --wavecar ../2.band/WAVECAR \
  --task kubo --bands 1:18

The explicit range selects the full trace and writes KUBO.csv automatically.
Its occupied-to-empty gap is finite at every stored point, including Gamma.
For a plotted example, follow examples/features/kubo-curvature/README.md.

# Historical command (retained for interpreting the archived BERRYCURV files)

The command below used the earlier individual-band behavior. The occupied
bands touch internally at Gamma; current single/per-band calculation rejects
those unresolved points instead of producing values and masking them later.
It is not a current reproduction command for the occupied-space trace.

# 1. copy WAVECAR file from ../2.band/WAVECAR

# 2. run berry curvature calculation with -kubo option
#    Note1: -kubo 2 option indicates that your k-point file is line mode.
#    Note2: -kp 1   option indicates that your result will not be repeated along the path
../../../../build/vaspberry-gfortran -f "../2.band/WAVECAR" \
  -kubo 2 -s 2 -kp 1

# 3. the results will be written in BERRYCURV_KUBO_... files.
#    Note that in BERRYCURV_KUBO.dat file contains total berry curvature.
